IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 7: subsection (c), the exclusion for taxpayers failing to meet certain requirements.
-- "Unforeseen circumstances" count only "to the extent provided in regulations", which are not among the sources: the caller says whether the reason counts.
-- The ratio is exact; the text does not round (fork F9).

§ `Subsection (c)(2): sales and exchanges to which the subsection applies`

-- src:63 | (i) a failure to meet the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), or
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(2)(A)(i) (src:63)
GIVEN `the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a) are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(2)(A)(i) subsection (a) would not apply by reason of a failure to meet the ownership and use requirements` MEANS
    `the opposite of` `the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a) are met`

-- src:64 | (ii) subsection (b)(3), and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(2)(A)(ii) (src:64)
GIVEN `subsection (b)(3) bars the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(2)(A)(ii) subsection (a) would not apply by reason of subsection (b)(3)` MEANS
    `subsection (b)(3) bars the sale`

-- src:62 | (A) subsection (a) would not (but for this subsection) apply to such sale or exchange by reason of—
-- src:63 | (i) a failure to meet the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), or
-- src:64 | (ii) subsection (b)(3), and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(2)(A) (src:62-64)
GIVEN `limb (i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(2)(A) subsection (a) would not (but for this subsection) apply by reason of (i) or (ii)` MEANS
    `either is true` `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`

-- (B): by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or (to the extent provided in regulations) unforeseen circumstances.
-- src:65 | (B) such sale or exchange is by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or, to the extent provided in regulations, unforeseen circumstances.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(2)(B) (src:65)
GIVEN `the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is by reason of health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is by reason of unforeseen circumstances, to the extent provided in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(2)(B) the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or unforeseen circumstances` MEANS
    IF    `the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment`
       OR `the sale is by reason of health`
       OR `the sale is by reason of unforeseen circumstances, to the extent provided in regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection shall apply to any sale or exchange if— ... (B) such sale or exchange is by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or, to the extent provided in regulations, unforeseen circumstances." (a failed "if"; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:60 | (2) Sales and exchanges to which subsection applies
-- src:61 | This subsection shall apply to any sale or exchange if—
-- src:62 | (A) subsection (a) would not (but for this subsection) apply to such sale or exchange by reason of—
-- src:63 | (i) a failure to meet the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), or
-- src:64 | (ii) subsection (b)(3), and
-- src:65 | (B) such sale or exchange is by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or, to the extent provided in regulations, unforeseen circumstances.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(2) (src:60-65)
GIVEN `limb (A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(2) this subsection applies to the sale or exchange` MEANS
    `both are true` `limb (A)` `limb (B)`

§ `Subsection (c)(1): in general`

-- (B)(i)(I): the aggregate of the periods in the 5-year period during which the property was owned AND used as the principal residence.
-- The text speaks here of one aggregate, so it is the days that are in both lists (fork F1: the one place where ownership and use must coincide).
-- src:57 | (I) the aggregate periods, during the 5-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence; or
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(I) (src:57)
GIVEN holding IS A Holding
      window IS A Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(I) the aggregate periods during the 5-year period the property has been owned and used as the principal residence` MEANS
    `the days in both lists inside the window` (holding's `periods of ownership`) (holding's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window

-- (B)(i)(II): the period after the date of the most recent prior sale to which (a) applied and before the date of this sale: the days strictly between.
-- src:58 | (II) the period after the date of the most recent prior sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied and before the date of such sale or exchange, bears to
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(II) (src:58)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      `the dates of prior sales or exchanges by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(II) the period after the most recent prior sale or exchange and before the date of such sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dates before the sale`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): with no prior sale to which (a) applied there is no such period, and the text does not say what the shorter of (I) and (II) is then.
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`the larger of` 0 (`the day number of` sale MINUS `the day number of` (latest d rest) MINUS 1))
    WHERE
        `the dates before the sale` MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD `the day number of` d AT MOST `the day number of` sale) `the dates of prior sales or exchanges by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied`
        latest d rest MEANS foldl (GIVEN best, x YIELD IF `the day number of` x AT LEAST `the day number of` best THEN x ELSE best) d rest

-- src:56 | (i) the shorter of—
-- src:57 | (I) the aggregate periods, during the 5-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence; or
-- src:58 | (II) the period after the date of the most recent prior sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied and before the date of such sale or exchange, bears to
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1)(B)(i) (src:56-58)
GIVEN `the aggregate periods (I)` IS A NUMBER
      `the period (II)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(c)(1)(B)(i) the shorter of (I) and (II)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period (II)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no period (II) exists; (I) alone is taken (fork F11).
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the aggregate periods (I)`
    WHEN JUST second THEN `the smaller of` `the aggregate periods (I)` second

-- src:59 | (ii) 2 years.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1)(B)(ii) (src:59)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(c)(1)(B)(ii) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` MEANS
    `the days in the years ending on` sale 2

-- (A) and (B): the dollar limitation is the amount that bears to the limitation (determined without regard to this paragraph) the ratio the shorter period bears to 2 years.
-- src:54 | (A) the amount which bears the same ratio to such limitation (determined without regard to this paragraph) as
-- src:55 | (B)
-- src:56 | (i) the shorter of—
-- src:57 | (I) the aggregate periods, during the 5-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence; or
-- src:58 | (II) the period after the date of the most recent prior sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied and before the date of such sale or exchange, bears to
-- src:59 | (ii) 2 years.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1)(A) (src:54-59)
GIVEN `the limitation determined without regard to this paragraph` IS A NUMBER
      `the shorter period` IS A NUMBER
      `2 years in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(c)(1) the dollar limitation as reduced` MEANS
    `the limitation determined without regard to this paragraph` TIMES (`the shorter period` DIVIDED BY `2 years in days`)

-- The first clause: in the case of a sale to which the subsection applies, the requirements and (b)(3) shall not apply.
-- src:53 | In the case of a sale or exchange to which this subsection applies, the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), and subsection (b)(3), shall not apply; but the dollar limitation under paragraph (1) or (2) of subsection (b), whichever is applicable, shall be equal to—
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(c)(1) (src:53)
GIVEN `subsection (c) applies to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(c)(1) the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), and subsection (b)(3), shall not apply to the sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `subsection (c) applies to the sale`
    WHEN JUST yes THEN
        IF yes
        -- The text's own words: "the ownership and use requirements of subsection (a), and subsection (b)(3), shall not apply" -- for a sale to which this subsection applies. JUST TRUE answers "they shall not apply".
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a sale or exchange to which this subsection applies"
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
